  "_summaryVsGrandTotalNote": "summary (from the deduplicated InboundCalls_Detailed file: 291 total/265 accepted/26 missed) reads 2 OVER the queue-level grandTotal (263 accepted/26 missed) \u2014 net of three effects: (1) two familiar direct-line-extension calls ('Crace Hotline', CallGUIDs 86267791\u2026 at 7:26:59 AM and c5829ddf\u2026 at 2:19:48 PM, both answered by Crace - Rec 1) \u2014 neither is one of the four named call queues, so neither appears in any CallQueue_Detailed file; (2) one genuinely unaccounted call with a normal 'YourGP' CallAlertName (CallGUID dcb5c29b\u2026, answered by Jasmine Deery at 5:05:55 PM) that does not appear in any of the three queue files supplied for this date \u2014 the recurring anomaly first seen 2026-10-23, then 27/28/30 and twice on 11-02, now its 6th distinct date (7th individual occurrence); (3) a NEW, opposite-direction wrinkle this date: one call (CallGUID 983f00a0\u2026, General Enquiries, 12:19:24 PM) is marked CallAnsweredInQueue=1 and credited to Rebecca Quinn in the queue CSV, but its InboundCalls_Detailed row shows a blank FirstUserName/TotalUniqueUsersCount=0 \u2014 so it counts toward grandTotal.accepted but NOT toward summary.accepted, pulling the gap down by 1. Net: +1+1+1-1 = +2, matching summary-minus-grandTotal exactly. Flagged distinctly rather than folded into either of the other two patterns, since it runs the opposite direction (grandTotal crediting a call summary does not).",
